  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Aleppo Equilibrium Pipeline Rehabilitation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NorCross&#x2019; main partner SARC is the primary provider of humanitarian services in Syria and has a lead operational role within the RCRC Movement, responding to the biggest humanitarian crisis in decades including in the provision of primary health care services, secondary and tertiary health care services as well as community-based health and care. In the area of health, SARC has recently signed an MoU with the Ministry of Health, assuring its special role in providing emergency health care and first aid.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Response EQ</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims at responding to the acute emergency WASH needs of the population affected by the earthquake in Aleppo City, Aleppo governorate. These will include vulnerable people affected by the earthquake and residing in various locations within the city. The project consists of rehabilitation of the equilibrium line.</narrative>
  </description>
